cad-model
=========

Two files in this skill are adapted, in modified form, from:

  Project:     AgentCAD 0.7.0
  Repository:  https://github.com/jdilla1277/agentcad
  Author:      James Dillard
  Source path: agentcad/helpers.py (safe_cut, safe_fuse, safe_intersection, _run_safe_boolean,
               _boolean_input, _canonical_occupied_shape, _volume_slack, _unwrap_shape,
               _rewrap_like)
  Copied:      2026-10-26, from the installed agentcad 0.7.0 wheel
  Licence:     Apache License, Version 2.0 (LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt, unmodified)

AgentCAD 0.7.0 ships no NOTICE file of its own; its licence is the unmodified Apache-2.0 text.
This project is licensed under MPL-2.0; the two adapted files keep Apache-2.0 and say so
in their SPDX headers.

Adapted files (Apache-2.0) and their modifications:
  scripts/cadmodel/safe.py
    1. safe_intersection(left, right) became safe_intersect(shape, *others), chaining COMMON
       over every input; an empty intersection is refused.
    2. safe_cut gained a lower bound: it cannot remove more than its tools' total volume.
    3. Results are re-wrapped for CadQuery 2.8 and build123d 0.13 without importing either
       kernel; AgentCAD's build123d compatibility classes are not carried over.
    4. Kernel warnings no longer raise Python warnings; refusals raise SafeEditError.
  scripts/cadmodel/occ_derived.py
    1. The non-destructive BOPAlgo_BOP runner (boolean), occupied-volume partition
       (occupied, BOPAlgo_CellsBuilder) and the 1e-7 relative volume slack (volume_slack),
       rewritten as kernel-neutral functions over raw TopoDS_Shape that run unchanged on
       OCP 7.9 (cadquery-ocp 7.9.3.1.1) and OCP 8.0 (cadquery-ocp-novtk 8.0.1.1.0).
       cadmodel.occ (MPL-2.0) re-exports them.

Ideas credited to AgentCAD in MPL-2.0 files (no AgentCAD code is copied there):
  scripts/cadmodel/check.py
    The sliver-face threshold SLIVER_FACE_MM2 = 1e-3 is AgentCAD's advisory value
    (agentcad/validation.py, _layer_advisory thresholds). LOOSE_TOLERANCE_MM was
    tightened from AgentCAD's 0.1 mm to 0.01 mm. Both stay advisory.
  scripts/cadmodel/diff.py
    _exact: shared / A-only / B-only volumes per part follow AgentCAD's
    exact-comparison method (agentcad/solid_compare.py, _canonicalize_occupied_volume: COMMON
    and both CUTs of occupied volumes), without its alignment, timeout workers, or approximate
    fallback.
